        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c366518d-5297-547c-8731-ebfa404f3f14",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Renée Montagne, Bob Edwards, Steve Inskeep, David Greene\n- Organizations: National Public Radio, Sirius XM Radio, Public Radio International, National Radio Hall of Fame\n- Products: Morning Edition, The Bob Edwards Show, Bob Edwards Weekend\n- Places: Culver City, California, Los Angeles\n- Roles: radio journalist, broadcast journalist, correspondent, host, co-host\n\nFacts:\n- Renée Montagne served as a National Public Radio correspondent and occasional host beginning in 1989.\n- In May 2004, Renée Montagne and Steve Inskeep succeeded longtime Morning Edition host Bob Edwards, initially as interim replacements.\n- Starting in 2004, Bob Edwards hosted The Bob Edwards Show on Sirius XM Radio and Bob Edwards Weekend, which Public Radio International distributed to more than 150 public radio stations.\n- In 2012, David Greene joined Renée Montagne and Steve Inskeep on National Public Radio's Morning Edition.\n- On November 11, 2016, Renée Montagne ended her tenure as co-host of National Public Radio's weekday morning news program Morning Edition.\n- Renée Montagne is an American radio journalist who usually broadcasts from NPR West in Culver City, California, a suburb of Los Angeles.\n- Bob Edwards, born May 16, 1947, is an American broadcast journalist, a Peabody Award-winning member of the National Radio Hall of Fame, and the first host of National Public Radio's flagship program Morning Edition.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "13f877d8-f6f7-5298-8f0a-d87eb0f93c5b",
        "text": "Page: Renée Montagne. Sentence: Renée Montagne (pronounced Mon-TAIN) is an American radio journalist and was the co-host (with Steve Inskeep and David Greene) of National Public Radio's weekday morning news program, \"Morning Edition\", from May 2004 to November 11, 2016.\nPage: Renée Montagne. Sentence: Montagne and Inskeep succeeded longtime host Bob Edwards, initially as interim replacements, and Greene joined the team in 2012.\nPage: Renée Montagne. Sentence: Montagne had served as a correspondent and occasional host since 1989.\nPage: Renée Montagne. Sentence: She usually broadcasts from NPR West in Culver City, California, a Los Angeles suburb.\nPage: Bob Edwards. Sentence: Robert Alan \"Bob\" Edwards (born May 16, 1947) is an American broadcast journalist, a Peabody Award-winning member of the National Radio Hall of Fame.\nPage: Bob Edwards. Sentence: He gained reputation as the first host of National Public Radio's flagship program, \"Morning Edition\".\nPage: Bob Edwards. Sentence: Starting in 2004, Edwards then was the host of \"The Bob Edwards Show\" on Sirius XM Radio and \"Bob Edwards Weekend\" distributed by Public Radio International to more than 150 public radio stations.",
